{
 "encounter_id": "00776",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Morning, doctor! I'm on a blood thinner, as you know, and I notice I bruise like a peach, so I thought I'd have it looked at. Nothing alarming, I don't think."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very sensible. Remind me which one, and how long you've taken it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Apixaban, 5 mg, twice a day. Since my operation last year, they put me on it for my irregular heartbeat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which operation was that?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A knee replacement, in March. The right one."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where are you getting bruises? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Forearms, mostly, from bumping into things, and a few on my shins. They look worse than they feel. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any nosebleeds, bleeding gums, or blood in your urine or stools?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that. No nosebleeds, no blood, no black stools."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any head injuries, or falls?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, no falls. I'm a sensible old thing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies, never."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anyone in the family with bleeding problems?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My mother bruised easily too, she was always covered in them."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you drink alcohol?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A glass of sherry in the evenings, no more."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your numbers. Pulse and pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Of course. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70 and irregular, blood pressure 130 over 76, temperature 36.5, oxygen 98 percent.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Irregular? Is that bad? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's your atrial fibrillation, as expected, and the rate is fine. Any breathlessness, chest pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, none whatsoever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Easy bruising on apixaban is common and usually harmless. I'd like to check a blood count and kidney function, because the dose depends on both."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Of course. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Don't stop the apixaban, it's protecting you from a stroke. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Understood. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Wear long sleeves when gardening, pad any sharp corners at home, and use a soft toothbrush."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll get some foam for the coffee table. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And avoid anti-inflammatory painkillers like ibuprofen, which increase bleeding risk."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I only take paracetamol. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's the right one. I'd like to see you again in four weeks, with the blood results."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Four weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
